ce.co cite34†Maojia Song ,\nL69: \nL70: cite35†Image cite36†Xinyu Wang ,\nL71: \nL72: [Button: Kuan Li] ,\nL73: cite37†Image†cdn-avatars.huggingface.co cite26†Jialong Wu ,\nL74: \nL75: cite38†Image cite39†Xuanzhong Chen ,\nL76: \nL77: [Button: Zile Qiao] ,\nL78: \nL79: cite40†Image cite41†Zhongwang Zhang ,\nL80: \nL81: [Button: Huifeng Yin] ,\nL82: \nL83: [Button: Shihao Cai] ,\nL84: \nL85: cite42†Image cite43†Runnan Fang ,\nL86: \nL87: [Button: Zhengwei Tao] ,\nL88: \nL89: cite44†Image cite45†Wenbiao Yin ,\nL90: \nL91: [Button: Chenxiong Qian] ,\nL92: \nL93: [Button: Yong Jiang] ,\nL94: \nL95: cite46†Image cite47†Pengjun Xie ,\nL96: \nL97: [Button: Fei Huang] ,\nL98: \nL99: [Button: Jingren Zhou]\nL100: ## Abstract\nL101: \nL102: AgentFounder, a deep research agent model incorporating Agentic Continual Pre-training, achieves state-of-the-art performance in agentic tasks while maintaining strong tool-use ability.\nL103: \nL104: Generated by cite48†Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct L105: cite49†Large language models (LLMs) have evolved into cite50†agentic systems capable of cite51†autonomous tool use and cite52†multi-step reasoning for complex problem-solving. However, cite53†post-training approaches building upon general-purpose foundation models consistently underperform in agentic tasks, particularly in open-source implementations.\nL106: We identify the root cause: the absence of robust agentic foundation models forces models during post-training to simultaneously learn diverse agentic behaviors while aligning them to expert demonstrations, thereby creating fundamental optimization tensions. To this end, we are the first to propose incorporating cite54†Agentic Continual Pre-training (Agentic CPT) into the cite55†deep research agents training pipeline to build powerful agentic foundational models.\nL107: Based on this approach, we develop a deep research agent model named cite56†AgentFounder . We evaluate our cite56†AgentFounder -30B on 10 benchmarks and achieve state-of-the-art performance while retains strong tool-use ability, notably 39.9% on cite57†BrowseComp-en , 43.3% on cite58†BrowseComp-zh , and 31.5% Pass@1 on cite59†HLE .\nL108: cite60†View arXiv page†arxiv.org cite61†View PDF†arxiv.org cite62†Project page†tongyi-agent.github.io cite63†GitHub 20k†github.com cite28†Add to collection L109: ### Community\nL110: \nL111: cite37†Image†cdn-avatars.huggingface.co L112: \nL113: cite26†callanwu L114: \nL115: Paper author Paper submitter cite64†Sep 17, 2025 L116: Large language models (LLMs) have evolved into agentic systems capable of autonomous tool use and multi-step reasoning for complex problem-solving. However, post-training approaches building upon general-purpose foundation models consistently underperform in agentic tasks, particularly in open-source implementations.\nL117: We identify the root cause: the absence of robust agentic foundation models forces models during post-training to simultaneously learn diverse agentic behaviors while aligning them to expert demonstrations, thereby creating fundamental optimization tensions. To this end, we are the first to propose incorporating Agentic Continual Pre-training (Agentic CPT) into the deep research agents training pipeline to build powerful agentic foundational models.\nL118: Based on this approach, we develop a deep research agent model named AgentFounder. We evaluate our AgentFounder-30B on 10 benchmarks and achieve state-of-the-art performance while retains strong tool-use ability, notably 39.9% on BrowseComp-en, 43.3% on BrowseComp-zh, and 31.5% Pass@1 on HLE.\nL119: Reply\nL120: \nL121: cite37†Image†cdn-avatars.huggingface.co L122: \nL123: cite26†callanwu L124: \nL125: Paper author Paper submitter cite65†Sep 17, 2025 L126: \nL127: Github: cite66†https://github.com/Alibaba-NLP/DeepResearch/†github.com L128: Blog: cite62†https://tongyi-agent.git