tFounder-30b\nL180: and\nL181: WebSailor-V2-30B-A3B\nL182: \nL183: are connected with:\nL184: Tongyi-DeepResearch-30B-A3B\nL185: \nL186: each of these agents is a separate model?\nL187: \nL188:   *   * [Button: 1 reply]\nL189: ·\nL190: \nL191: cite29†Image L192: \nL193: cite30†HKU-Liangcai L194: \nL195: Paper author cite86†Sep 21, 2025 L196: Thanks for your attention. Actually, Tongyi DeepResearch adopts the methods and data from AgentFounder and WebSailor-v2. A more detailed version will be included in our future technical reports (when available). However, the data and models used in AgentFounder and WebSailor-v2 may be derived from exploratory experiments and may differ from the final DeepResearch model.\nL197: \nL198: [Input: Reply in thread]\nL199: \nL200: cite87†Image†cdn-avatars.huggingface.co L201: \nL202: cite88†yczhuang L203: \nL204: cite89†Sep 19, 2025 L205: Thank you for sharing this very interesting paper! Very cool work! We have done some similar exploration of using CPT for agent training previously: cite90†https://arxiv.org/pdf/2502.06589†arxiv.org and have some similar findings. It is great to see the performance further boosted with stronger models (Qwen-series) and larger amount of data.\nL206: \nL207:   *   * [Button: 2 replies]\nL208: ·\nL209: \nL210: cite29†Image L211: \nL212: cite30†HKU-Liangcai L213: \nL214: Paper author cite91†Sep 21, 2025 L215: Pretty Cool! I didn't notice this paper before, I will read your work carefully, and I think it is very likely that we need to cite your work in the updated version!! Thank you for your reply!!!\nL216: \nL217: Expand 1 reply\nL218: \nL219: [Input: Reply in thread]\nL220: \nL221: [Button: Edit][Button: Preview]\nL222: \nL223: Upload images, audio, and videos by dragging in the text input, pasting, or clicking here.\nL224: \nL225: Tap or paste here to upload images\nL226: \nL227: Comment\nL228: \nL229: cite92†Sign up or cite28†log in to comment\nL230: \nL231: Get thi