rprise L8:   * cite6†Pricing L9:   *     * Website\nL10: \nL11:       * cite7†Tasks L12:       * cite8†HuggingChat L13:       * cite9†Collections L14:       * cite10†Languages L15:       * cite11†Organizations L16:     * Community\nL17:       * cite12†Blog L18:       * cite13†Posts L19:       * cite14†Daily Papers L20:       * cite15†Hardware L21:       * cite16†Learn L22:       * cite17†Discord L23:       * cite18†Forum†discuss.huggingface.co L24:       * cite19†GitHub†github.com L25:     * Solutions\nL26: \nL27:       * cite5†Team & Enterprise L28:       * cite20†Hugging Face PRO L29:       * cite21†Enterprise Support L30:       * cite22†Inference Providers L31:       * cite23†Inference Endpoints L32:       * cite3†Storage Buckets L33: \nL34:   * * * *\nL35: \nL36:   * cite24†Log In L37:   * cite25†Sign Up L38: \nL39: cite14†Papers L40: \nL41: arxiv:2509.13312\nL42: \nL43: Copy markdown\nL44: # WebWeaver: Structuring Web-Scale Evidence with Dynamic Outlines for Open-Ended Deep Research\nL45: \nL46: Published on Sep 16, 2025\nL47: \nL48: · Submitted by cite26†taesiri on Sep 17, 2025\nL49: \nL50: cite27†#2 Paper of the day L51: \nL52: cite28†Upvote 107 L53: \nL54:   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   * [Button: +99]\nL55: \nL56: Authors:\nL57: \nL58: cite29†Image cite30†Zijian Li ,\nL59: \nL60: cite31†Image cite32†Xin Guan ,\nL61: \nL62: [Button: Bo Zhang] ,\nL63: \nL64: [Button: Shen Huang] ,\nL65: \nL66: [Button: Houquan Zhou] ,\nL67: \nL68: [Button: Shaopeng Lai] ,\nL69: \nL70: [Button: Ming Yan] ,\nL71: \nL72: [Button: Yong Jiang] ,\nL73: \nL74: cite33†Image cite34†Pengjun Xie ,\nL75: [Button: Fei Huang] ,\nL76: \nL77: [Button: Jun Zhang] ,\nL78: \nL79: cite35†Image cite36†Jingren Zhou L80: ## Abstract\nL81: \nL82: WebWeaver, a dual-agent framework, addresses open-ended deep research challenges by integrating adaptive planning and focused synthesis to produce high-quality, reliable reports.\nL83: \nL84: Generated by cite37†Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct L85: This paper tackles cite38†open-ended deep research (OEDR), a complex challenge where cite39†AI agents must synthesize vast web-scale information into insightful reports. Current approaches are plagued by dual-fold limitations: static research pipelines that decouple planning from cite40†evidence acquisition and one-shot generation paradigms that easily suffer from cite41†long-context failure issues like \"cite42†loss in the middle \" and cite43†hallucinations .\nL86: To address these challenges, we introduce WebWeaver, a novel cite44†dual-agent framework that emulates the human research process. The cite45†planner operates in a dynamic cycle, iteratively interleaving cite40†evidence acquisition with cite46†outline optimization to produce a comprehensive, source-grounded outline linking to a cite47†memory bank of evidence. The cite48†writer then executes a cite49†hierarchical retrieval and cite50†writing process , composing the report section by section.\nL87: By performing targeted retrieval of only the necessary evidence from the cite47†memory bank for each part, it effectively mitigates long-context issues. Our framework establishes a new state-of-the-art across major OEDR benchmarks, including cite51†DeepResearch Bench , cite52†DeepConsult , and cite53†DeepResearchGym .\nL88: These results validate our human-centric, iterative methodology, demonstrating that adaptive planning and focused synthesis are crucial for producing high-quality, reliable, and well-structured reports.\nL89: cite54†View arXiv page†arxiv.org cite55†View PDF†arxiv.org cite56†Project page†tongyi-agent.github.io cite28†Add to collection L90: ### Community\nL91: \nL92: cite57†Image†cdn-avatars.huggingface.co L93: \nL94: cite26†taesiri L95: \nL96: Paper submitter cite58†Sep 17, 2025 L97: This paper tackles open-ended deep research (OEDR), a complex challenge where AI agents must synthesize vast web-scale information into insightful reports. Current approaches are plagued by dual-fold limitations: static research pipelines that decouple planning from evidence acquisition and one-shot generation paradigms that easily suffer from long-context failure issues like \"loss in the middle\" and hallucinations.\nL98: To address these challenges, we introduce WebWeaver, a novel dual-agent framework that emulates the human research process. The planner operates in a dynamic cycle, iteratively interleaving evidence acquisition with outline optimization to produce a comprehensive, source-grounded outline linking to a memory bank of evidence. The writer then executes a hierarchical retrieval and writing process, composing the report section by section.\nL99: By performing targeted retrieval of only the necessary evidence from the memory bank for each part, it effectively mitigates long-context issues. Our framework establishes a new state-of-the-art across major OEDR benchmarks, including DeepResearch Bench, DeepConsult, and DeepResearchGym. These results validate our human-centric, iterative methodology, demonstrating that adaptive planning and focused synthesis are crucial for producing high-quality, reliable, and well-structured reports.\nL100: Reply\nL101: \nL102: cite59†Image L103: \nL104: cite60†Ehaschia L105: \nL106: cite61†Sep 17, 2025 L107: \nL108: Github: cite62†https://github.com/Alibaba-NLP/DeepResearch/†github.com L109: Blog: cite56†https://tongyi-agent.github.io/blog/†tongyi-agent.github.io L110: \nL111: Reply\nL112: \nL113: cite63†Image†cdn-avatars.huggingface.co L114: \nL115: cite64†librarian-bot L116: \nL117: cite65†Sep 18, 2025 L118: \nL119: This is an automated message from the cite66†Librarian Bot . I found the following papers similar to this paper.\nL120: \nL121: The following papers were recommended by the Semantic Scholar API\nL122:   * cite67†Web