* cite10†Languages L15:       * cite11†Organizations L16:     * Community\nL17:       * cite12†Blog L18:       * cite13†Posts L19:       * cite14†Daily Papers L20:       * cite15†Hardware L21:       * cite16†Learn L22:       * cite17†Discord L23:       * cite18†Forum†discuss.huggingface.co L24:       * cite19†GitHub†github.com L25:     * Solutions\nL26: \nL27:       * cite5†Team & Enterprise L28:       * cite20†Hugging Face PRO L29:       * cite21†Enterprise Support L30:       * cite22†Inference Providers L31:       * cite23†Inference Endpoints L32:       * cite3†Storage Buckets L33: \nL34:   * * * *\nL35: \nL36:   * cite24†Log In L37:   * cite25†Sign Up L38: \nL39: cite14†Papers L40: \nL41: arxiv:2509.13305\nL42: \nL43: Copy markdown\nL44: # WebSailor-V2: Bridging the Chasm to Proprietary Agents via Synthetic Data and Scalable Reinforcement Learning\nL45: \nL46: Published on Sep 16, 2025\nL47: \nL48: · Submitted by cite26†Jialong Wu on Sep 17, 2025\nL49: \nL50: cite27†#3 Paper of the day L51: \nL52: cite28†Upvote 93 L53: \nL54:   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   * [Button: +85]\nL55: \nL56: Authors:\nL57: \nL58: [Button: Kuan Li] ,\nL59: \nL60: cite29†Image cite30†Zhongwang Zhang ,\nL61: \nL62: [Button: Huifeng Yin] ,\nL63: \nL64: cite31†Image cite32†Rui Ye ,\nL65: \nL66: cite33†Image cite34†Yida Zhao ,\nL67: \nL68: [Button: Liwen Zhang] ,\nL69: \nL70: cite35†Image†cdn-avatars.huggingface.co cite36†Litu Ou ,\nL71: [Button: Dingchu Zhang] ,\nL72: \nL73: cite37†Image cite38†Xixi Wu ,\nL74: \nL75: cite39†Image†cdn-avatars.huggingface.co cite26†Jialong Wu ,\nL76: \nL77: cite40†Image cite41†Xinyu Wang ,\nL78: \nL79: [Button: Zile Qiao] ,\nL80: \nL81: [Button: Zhen Zhang] ,\nL82: \nL83: [Button: Yong Jiang] ,\nL84: \nL85: cite42†Image cite43†Pengjun Xie ,\nL86: \nL87: [Button: Fei Huang] ,\nL88: \nL89: [Button: Jingren Zhou]\nL90: ## Abstract\nL91: \nL92: WebSailor, a post-training methodology, enhances open-source models with systematic uncertainty reduction, matching proprietary agents' performance in complex information-seeking tasks.\nL93: \nL94: Generated by cite44†Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct L95: Transcending human cognitive limitations represents a critical frontier in cite45†LLM training . Proprietary agentic systems like cite46†DeepResearch have demonstrated superhuman capabilities on extremely complex information-seeking benchmarks such as cite47†BrowseComp , a feat previously unattainable. We posit that their success hinges on a sophisticated cite48†reasoning pattern absent in open-source models: the ability to systematically reduce extreme uncertainty when navigating vast information landscapes.\nL96: Based on this insight, we introduce WebSailor, a complete post-training methodology designed to instill this crucial capability. Our approach involves generating novel, cite49†high-uncertainty tasks through cite50†structured sampling and cite51†information obfuscation , cite52†RFT cold start , and an efficient cite53†agentic RL training algorithm, Duplicating Sampling Policy Optimization (cite54†DUPO ).\nL97: With this integrated pipeline, WebSailor significantly outperforms all open-source agents in complex information-seeking tasks, matching proprietary agents' performance and closing the capability gap.\nL98: cite55†View arXiv page†arxiv.org cite56†View PDF†arxiv.org cite57†Project page†tongyi-agent.github.io cite28†Add to collection L99: ### Community\nL100: \nL101: cite39†Image†cdn-avatars.huggingface.co L102: \nL103: cite26†callanwu L104: \nL105: Paper author Paper submitter cite58†Sep 17, 2025 L106: To significantly advance the capabilities of open-source web agents, we present WebSailor-V2, a complete post-training pipeline encompassing data construction, Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT), and Reinforcement Learning (RL). Our methodology features two key innovations: (1) On the data front, we developed SailorFog-QA-2, a novel dataset built from a densely interconnected knowledge graph that introduces a wide variety of uncertainties beyond simple obfuscation, fostering more sophisticated reasoning.\nL107: (2) For training, we engineered a dual-environment RL framework, combining a high-fidelity simulator for rapid, low-cost algorithmic iteration with a robust, managed real-world environment for stable final policy training, all integrated within a symbiotic data-policy feedback loop. Trained on the Qwen3-30B-A3B model, WebSailorV2 achieves state-of-the-art results, scoring 35.3 on BrowseComp-EN, 44.1 on BrowseComp-ZH, and 30.6 on Humanity’s Last Exam (HLE).\nL108: Notably, our 30B-A3B MOE agent significantly outperforms all existing open-source agents and surpasses even the 671B DeepSeek-V3.1, demonstrating performance competitive with leading proprietary systems.\nL109: Reply\nL110: \nL111: cite39†Image†cdn-avatars.huggingface.co L112: \nL113: cite26†callanwu L114: \nL115: Paper author Paper submitter cite59†Sep 17, 2025 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPaper page - ReSum: Unlocking Long-Horizon Search Intelligence via Context Summarization (https://huggingface.co/papers/2509.13313)\nciteturn3239view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn3237view0\",\"id\":40}); Total lines: 213\n"
